# T38407 — VLAN translation - basic functionality — tb470 IE520 stack — 2026-09-30 — PASS

Verdict: PASS. Step 1 (configure VLAN translation) was accepted and read back. Step 2: tagged
traffic matching the rule left the DUT with the translated VLAN-ID, 100/100. Proof on the wire at a
host behind the egress port, and in the mirror of the egress port (the case's observation method).
The translation also worked in reverse and on an egress-side rule (100/100 each). With the feature
OFF, the same wire VID was dropped (0/100). Run labelled: clean (one mirror stage was invalid and
re-run; see m2 below).

Operator: bench-runner subagent (sentinel = parent session, /test-mode shape A), Terrence away.
Queue: IE520/CAMPAIGN-QUEUE-2026-09-29.md row 7. Case text: ck.db AWPTCM-T38407, 2 steps: "Configure
VLAN translation on the DUT"; "Send tagged traffic into the DUT that matches the VLAN translation rule
and mirror the egress port" → "The traffic leaving the DUT should have the translated VLAN-ID". No
objective or precondition text.

