## Two CLI behaviours met on the way (recorded, not graded)
1. Entering a mirror test port's interface mode prints a `%` caution line:
   `% port1.0.9 is currently configured as a mirror-port. Use caution when altering its config`. The
   first m2 reconfiguration (16:36:46) stopped there under `--stop-on-error`. It was redone at 16:37:32
   with the caution accepted and every other line checked. No other `% ` line appeared (that try's
   output file was overwritten by the redo, and the raw text is in tb470 /tmp/ckvlan3/console-u5.log).
2. On the mirror port, `no mirror interface port1.0.13` + `mirror interface port1.0.2 …` removed the port's
   `switchport access vlan 3992` line. `show running-config interface port1.0.9` then read only
   `switchport` / `switchport mode access` / `mirror interface port1.0.2 direction transmit`. The
   teardown re-added `switchport access vlan 3992`.

